1
00:00:01,879 --> 00:00:03,878
Chapter 92.

2
00:00:03,879 --> 00:00:06,359
Amberress.

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:11,719
Now, this amberress is a very curious substance and so important as an article

4
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:17,795
of commerce that in 1791 a certain Nantucketborn captain coffin was

5
00:00:17,796 --> 00:00:23,079
examined at the bar of the English House of Commons on the subject. For at that

6
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:28,198
time, and indeed until a comparatively late day, the precise origin of

7
00:00:28,199 --> 00:00:34,039
amberress remained like amber itself a problem to the learned. Though the word

8
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:39,878
amberress is but a French compound for gray amber, yet the two substances are

9
00:00:39,879 --> 00:00:45,399
quite distinct. For amber, though at times found on the sea coast, is also

10
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:51,399
dug up in some far inland soils, whereas amberress is never found except upon the

11
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:57,558
sea. Besides, amber is a hard, transparent, brittle, odorless substance

12
00:00:57,559 --> 00:01:04,115
used for mouthpieces to pipes, for beads and ornaments. But amberress is soft,

13
00:01:04,116 --> 00:01:10,679
waxy and so highly fragrant and spicy that it is largely used in perfumery in

14
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:17,238
pastels, precious candles, hair powders and pomatum. The Turks use it in cooking

15
00:01:17,239 --> 00:01:22,115
and also carry it to Mecca for the same purpose that frankincense is carried to

16
00:01:22,116 --> 00:01:29,159
St. Peter's in Rome. Some wine merchants drop a few grains into clarret to flavor it.

17
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:33,159
Who would think then that such fine ladies and gentlemen should regail

18
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:39,079
themselves with an essence found in the inglorious bowels of a sick whale? Yet

19
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:44,755
so it is. By some amberress is supposed to be the cause and by others the effect

20
00:01:44,756 --> 00:01:49,795
of the disyspsia in the whale. How to cure such a disspyspsia? It were hard to

21
00:01:49,796 --> 00:01:55,634
say, unless by administering three or four boatloads of brandth pills, and

22
00:01:55,635 --> 00:02:01,079
then running out of harm's way, as laborers do in blasting rocks.

23
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:05,878
I have forgotten to say that there were found in this amberress certain hard

24
00:02:05,879 --> 00:02:11,079
round bony plates which at first Stub thought might be sailor's trousers

25
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:15,079
buttons, but afterwards it turned out that they were nothing more than pieces

26
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:19,878
of small squid bones inbalmed in that manner.

27
00:02:19,879 --> 00:02:24,359
Now that the incorruption of this most fragrant amberress should be found in

28
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:29,479
the heart of such decay, is this nothing? Beth think thee of that saying

29
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:34,755
of St. Paul in Corinthians about corruption and incorruption. How that we

30
00:02:34,756 --> 00:02:40,039
are sown in dishonor but raised in glory. And likewise call to mind that

31
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:45,795
saying of paracelus about what it is that maketh the best musk. Also forget

32
00:02:45,796 --> 00:02:51,238
not the strange fact that of all things of ill savor, cologne water in its

33
00:02:51,239 --> 00:02:56,039
rudimental manufacturing stages is the worst.

34
00:02:56,040 --> 00:03:00,914
I should like to conclude the chapter with the above appeal, but cannot, owing

35
00:03:00,915 --> 00:03:06,359
to my anxiety to repel a charge often made against Whaleman, and which, in the

36
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:11,719
estimation of some already biased minds, might be considered as indirectly

37
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:16,999
substantiated by what has been said of the Frenchman's two whales. Elsewhere in

38
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:21,795
this volume, the slanderous espersion has been disproved, that the vocation of

39
00:03:21,796 --> 00:03:26,838
whailing is throughout a slatterly untidy business. But there is another

40
00:03:26,839 --> 00:03:32,274
thing to rebut. They hint that all whales always smell bad. Now, how did

41
00:03:32,275 --> 00:03:35,318
this odious stigma originate?

42
00:03:35,319 --> 00:03:39,719
I upon that it is plainly traceable to the first arrival of the Greenland

43
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:45,399
whailing ships in London more than two centuries ago. Because those whalemen

44
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:50,679
did not then and do not now try out their oil at sea as the southern ships

45
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:55,558
have always done, but cutting up the fresh blubber into small bits, thrust it

46
00:03:55,559 --> 00:04:00,594
through the bung holes of large casks, and carry it home in that manner. The

47
00:04:00,595 --> 00:04:04,999
shortness of the season in those icy seas and the sudden and violent storms

48
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,954
to which they are exposed forbidding any other course. The consequence is that

49
00:04:09,955 --> 00:04:14,518
upon breaking into the hold and unloading one of these whale cemeteries

50
00:04:14,519 --> 00:04:19,634
in the Greenland dock, a saver is given forth somewhat similar to that arising

51
00:04:19,635 --> 00:04:26,274
from excavating an old city graveyard for the foundations of a lying hospital.

52
00:04:26,275 --> 00:04:31,238
I partly surmise also that this wicked charge against whalers may be likewise

53
00:04:31,239 --> 00:04:36,594
imputed to the existence on the coast of Greenland in former times of a Dutch

54
00:04:36,595 --> 00:04:41,634
village called Schmearrenburgg or Smeirnberg which latter name is the one

55
00:04:41,635 --> 00:04:47,318
used by the learned Fogo von Slack in his great work on smells a textbook on

56
00:04:47,319 --> 00:04:54,518
that subject as its name imports smear fat berg to put up this village was

57
00:04:54,519 --> 00:04:58,914
founded in order to afford a place for the blubber of the Dutch whale fleet to

58
00:04:58,915 --> 00:05:04,198
be tried out without being taken home to Holland for that purpose. It was a

59
00:05:04,199 --> 00:05:09,399
collection of furnaces, fat kettles, and oil sheds, and when the works were in

60
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:14,755
full operation, certainly gave forth no very pleasant savor. But all this is

61
00:05:14,756 --> 00:05:19,719
quite different with a South Sea sperm whaler, which in a voyage of four years,

62
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:24,914
perhaps after completely filling her hold with oil, does not perhaps consume

63
00:05:24,915 --> 00:05:30,274
50 days in the business of boiling out, and in the state that it is cast, the

64
00:05:30,275 --> 00:05:35,954
oil is nearly scentless. The truth is that living or dead, if but decently

65
00:05:35,955 --> 00:05:41,558
treated, whales as a species, are by no means creatures of ill odor. Nor can

66
00:05:41,559 --> 00:05:46,518
whaleman be recognized as the people of the Middle Ages affected to detect a Jew

67
00:05:46,519 --> 00:05:52,594
in the company by the nose. Nor indeed can the whale possibly be otherwise than

68
00:05:52,595 --> 00:05:57,634
fragrant, when, as a general thing he enjoys such high health, taking

69
00:05:57,635 --> 00:06:02,914
abundance of exercise, always out ofdoors, though it is true, seldom in

70
00:06:02,915 --> 00:06:08,679
the open air. I say that the motion of a sperm whale's flukes above water,

71
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:13,634
dispenses a perfume, as when a muskscented lady rustles her dress in a

72
00:06:13,635 --> 00:06:18,914
warm parlor. What then shall I liken the sperm whale to for fragrance considering

73
00:06:18,915 --> 00:06:24,594
his magnitude? Must it not be to that famous elephant with jeweled tusks and

74
00:06:24,595 --> 00:06:33,199
redolent with myrr, which was led out of an Indian town to do honor to Alexander the Great.
